SCOPE NOTE
----------
This file reports.  It repairs nothing.  Items 1-3 are mechanical fixes and
are deliberately left to the owner: the kernel entry file's §0(4) names
"correctly recognising the work as advanced, then proposing to verify,
consolidate or tidy something" as this repository's measured failure mode for
arriving agents, and it is right that repair is not the work.  But §0(4) is
about substituting tidying for creation.  It is not a licence to publish
"every claim is a term a typechecker accepts or refuses" over a tree where no
typechecker runs.  Verification is not the work; it is the precondition for
believing the work, and it is currently unavailable to every reader.
